window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f47b3f97f09c0b11"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"analyze-datasets-and-ship-reports\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">分析数据集并交付报告</h1> <p>把杂乱数据转化为清晰的分析和可视化结果。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT Work 清理数据、合并来源、围绕问题开展探索、建立模型并制作清晰的报告，同时说明支持性图表和注意事项。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>从杂乱文件开始，最后产出图表、备忘录、仪表盘或报告的数据分析。</li> <li>需要清理数据、可靠合并、可解释模型或可复现分析的问题。</li> <li>需要其他人能够审阅和复用交付成果的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查 CSV、TSV 和 Excel 文件，核查公式与合并操作，并创建便于审阅的表格或图表。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取你在 Drive 中指定且获准使用的 Google Sheets 和来源文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Data Analytics</td> <td>收集来源背景、分析并验证数据，以及构建可复用的报告、仪表盘、图表或笔记本。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>分析工具栈</td> <td><a href=\"https://pandas.pydata.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pandas（需联网）</a> 搭配 <a href=\"https://matplotlib.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">matplotlib（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://seaborn.pydata.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">seaborn（需联网）</a></td> <td>适合作为导入、数据概况分析、合并、清理和初步绘图的默认工具。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>建模</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.statsmodels.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">statsmodels（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scikit-learn（需联网）</a></td> <td>先从可解释的基线模型开始，再考虑更复杂的预测模型。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">起步提示词</h2> <p>将数据整理成有来源依据的报告</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 @Data Analytics 检查我附上的房屋销售数据集和距高速公路距离数据集，判断靠近高速公路的房屋是否更便宜。\n\n说明每个来源包含什么内容，找出相关列和可能的合并键，并检查缺失值、重复项、无法匹配的记录和不完整数据。清理并合并输入数据，但不要覆盖来源文件，也不要编造数值。\n\n使用清晰的图表探索问题；只有在建模有帮助时才从可解释的模型开始，并用通俗语言说明结果、假设和不确定性。请提供简洁的报告、笔记本或电子表格，先给出答案，注明创建的文件名称，并指出任何可能改变结论的数据问题。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">简介</h2> <p>数据分析的核心，是利用数据为决策提供依据。分析本身不是目的，最终要产出能帮助他人采取行动的成果：供管理层查看的图表、产品团队的实验结果、研究人员的模型评估，或指导日常运营的仪表盘。</p> <p>《R for Data Science》推广过一个实用框架：先导入并整理数据，再不断循环进行转换、可视化和建模，在形成认识后传达结果。</p> <p>ChatGPT Work 很适合参与这一流程。它可以帮助你清理数据、探索假设、生成分析，并制作可复现的成果。目标不应只是一次性的笔记本，而应是其他人能够审阅、信任并重新运行的分析。</p> <p><a id=\"define-your-use-case\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">明确你的使用场景</h2> <p>先选定一个要用数据回答的具体问题。问题越具体，越容易确定所需输入、检查项和结果。</p> <p><a id=\"running-example-property-values-near-the-highway\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">示例：高速公路附近的房屋估值</h3> <p>例如，我们要探索以下问题：</p> <blockquote> <p>高速公路附近的房屋，其估值会低多少？</p> </blockquote> <p>假设一个数据集包含房屋估值或成交价格，另一个包含位置、地块或与高速公路距离的信息。工作不只是运行一个模型，还要确保输入数据可信、记录合并方法、检验结果的稳健性，并产出其他人可以使用的成果。</p> <p>你可以附上 CSV 或 Excel 工作簿；也可以使用 <code>@google-drive</code> 指定一份获准使用的 Google Sheet，或在电脑上存有数据时使用桌面应用。</p> <p><a id=\"example-result\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">示例结果</h3> <p>在一个虚构示例中，ChatGPT 将 11 笔房屋交易与高速公路距离文件匹配，并标记出 1 笔找不到对应距离的交易。距离高速公路 1 英里以内的房屋平均售价为 <strong>$500,000</strong>，而距离 2 到 5 英里的房屋平均售价为 <strong>$600,000</strong>。</p> <p>排除价格最高的远距离房屋后，两组之间的差额仍为 <strong>$94,000</strong>。报告和图表会说明样本量较小、未匹配的交易已排除，而且这种比较不能证明因果关系，也没有控制街区、成交时间、交通或噪声等因素。</p> <p><a id=\"import-the-data\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">导入数据</h2> <p>先附上文件，并请 ChatGPT 检查它们。这有助于回答一些基础但重要的问题：</p> <ul> <li>这些文件是什么格式？</li> <li>每个数据集看起来代表什么？</li> <li>哪些列可能是目标值、标识符、日期、地点或度量值？</li> <li>有哪些明显的数据质量问题？</li> </ul> <p>暂时不要询问结论。先让 ChatGPT 列出数据清单并作出说明。</p> <p><a id=\"tidy-and-merge-the-inputs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">整理并合并输入数据</h2> <p>大多数真实工作都从这里开始：你有两个或更多数据集，主键不明确，而直接合并可能会丢失数据或产生重复记录。</p> <p>让 ChatGPT 在执行合并前先检查方案：</p> <ul> <li>检查候选键是否唯一。</li> <li>统计空值比例和格式差异。</li> <li>规范明显的格式问题，例如大小写、空格或地址格式。</li> <li>试运行合并并报告匹配率。</li> <li>写入最终合并文件之前，先建议最安全的合并策略。</li> </ul> <p>如果需要推导最佳键，例如标准化地址、由多列组合而成的地块标识符，或位置关联键，请先让 ChatGPT 解释其中的取舍和边界情况，再决定是否接受该合并。</p> <p><a id=\"explore-with-charts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">用图表探索数据</h2> <p>先用图表了解数据，再决定要选择什么模型。在高速公路的例子中，可以比较公路附近和较远房屋，检查异常值和缺失值模式，并确认表面上的影响是否其实来自街区构成、房屋面积或其他因素。</p> <p>让每张图都围绕原始问题展开。保存有用的比较结果，方便其他人检查分析。</p> <p><a id=\"model-the-question\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">为问题建立模型</h2> <p>不是每项分析都需要复杂模型。先从容易解释的基线模型开始。</p> <p>针对高速公路问题，一个合理的初步方案是使用回归或其他透明模型，估计高速公路距离与房屋价值之间的关系，同时控制面积、房龄和位置等相关因素。</p> <p>请 ChatGPT 明确说明：</p> <ul> <li>目标变量和特征的定义。</li> <li>纳入哪些控制变量以及原因。</li> <li>数据泄漏风险和排除项。</li> <li>如何选择数据拆分、评估方式或不确定性估计。</li> <li>如何用通俗语言解释结果。</li> </ul> <p>如果第一个模型效果不佳，仍然能带来有用信息。它可以帮助你判断问题出在模型、特征、合并质量，还是问题本身。</p> <p><a id=\"communicate-the-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">传达分析结果</h2> <p>只有其他人能够使用，分析才有价值。请 ChatGPT 按受众需要的形式制作成果：</p> <ul> <li>提供给技术协作者的 Markdown 备忘录。</li> <li>供后续运营使用的电子表格或 CSV。</li> <li>面向决策者的格式化文档或 PDF。</li> <li>可复用分析所需的笔记本、仪表盘或静态报告。</li> </ul> <p>请它同时说明注意事项。如果合并质量不理想、存在抽样偏差，或模型假设不够稳固，交付内容就应明确说明。</p> <p><a id=\"optional-set-up-a-python-environment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"python\">可选：设置 Python 环境</h2> <p>如果项目需要可复用的脚本或笔记本，请 ChatGPT 使用现有 Python 环境，或搭建一个小型、可复现的环境。保持来源文件不变，把分析结果、图表和最终报告另存。使用 ChatGPT Work 分析已附加的文件之前，不必先设置 Python。</p> <p><a id=\"suggested-prompts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_16\">建议提示词</h2> <p><strong>载入数据集并进行说明</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the data files I've attached and explain what each one contains. Identify likely target columns, dates, parcel or location identifiers, file formats, missing information, and obvious quality issues. Don't draw conclusions yet.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">检查我附上的数据文件，并解释每个文件包含什么。识别可能的目标列、日期、地块或位置标识符、文件格式、缺失信息，以及明显的数据质量问题。暂时不要下结论。</div></div> <p><strong>合并前先检查方案</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check how these datasets should be joined. Profile the candidate keys, show duplicate and unmatched records, normalize obvious formatting issues, and explain the safest join. Don't invent missing values or overwrite the source files.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">检查应该如何关联这些数据集。分析候选关联键的特征，展示重复记录和未匹配记录，统一明显不一致的格式，并解释最稳妥的关联方式。不要编造缺失值，也不要覆盖源文件。</div></div> <p><strong>建立第一个可解释模型</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Model whether highway proximity is associated with lower property values. Start with an interpretable baseline, account for home size, age, and neighborhood where the data supports it, and explain the effect, uncertainty, and limitations in plain language.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">建立模型，分析靠近高速公路是否与较低的房产价值相关。从可解释的基准模型开始，在数据支持的情况下纳入房屋面积、房龄和街区因素，并用通俗语言解释影响、不确定性和局限。</div></div> <p><strong>为利益相关方整理结果</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this analysis into a short, stakeholder-ready report. Put the answer first, include the most useful supporting charts, explain the data and join checks, and clearly flag any limitations or uncertainty. Keep the source data unchanged and name the files you create.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">将这项分析整理成一份简短、可交给利益相关方的报告。先给出答案，加入最有用的支持性图表，解释数据检查和关联检查，并明确指出任何局限或不确定性。保持源数据不变，并说明你创建的文件名称。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"analyze-datasets-and-ship-reports\">Analyze datasets and ship reports</h1> <p>Turn messy data into clear analysis and visualizations.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT Work to clean data, join sources, explore a question, model the result, and produce a clear report with supporting charts and caveats.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Data analysis that starts with messy files and ends with a chart, memo, dashboard, or report.</li> <li>Questions that require cleaning, reliable joins, interpretable models, or reproducible analysis.</li> <li>Teams that need artifacts others can review and reuse.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect CSV, TSV, and Excel files, check formulas and joins, and create reviewable tables or charts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read the approved Google Sheets and source files you name in Drive.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Data Analytics</td> <td>Gather source context, analyze and validate data, and build reusable reports, dashboards, charts, or notebooks.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Analysis stack</td> <td><a href=\"https://pandas.pydata.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pandas (online)</a> with <a href=\"https://matplotlib.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">matplotlib (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://seaborn.pydata.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">seaborn (online)</a></td> <td>Good defaults for import, profiling, joins, cleaning, and the first round of charts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Modeling</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.statsmodels.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">statsmodels (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scikit-learn (online)</a></td> <td>Start with interpretable baselines before moving to more complex predictive models.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Turn data into a source-backed report</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Data Analytics to inspect the attached property-sales and highway-distance datasets and determine whether homes near the highway have lower property values.\n\nExplain what each source contains, identify the relevant columns and likely join keys, and check for missing values, duplicates, unmatched records, and incomplete data. Clean and join the inputs without overwriting the source files or inventing values.\n\nExplore the question with clear supporting charts, start with an interpretable model when modeling is useful, and explain the result, assumptions, and uncertainty in plain language. Return a concise report, notebook, or spreadsheet with the answer first, name the files you create, and flag any data issue that could change the conclusion.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>At its core, data analysis is about using data to inform decisions. The goal isn't analysis for its own sake. It's to produce an artifact that helps someone act: a chart for leadership, an experiment readout for a product team, a model evaluation for researchers, or a dashboard that guides daily operations.</p> <p>A useful framework, popularized by <em>R for Data Science</em>, is a loop: import and tidy data, then iterate between transform, visualize, and model to build understanding before you communicate results.</p> <p>ChatGPT Work fits well into this workflow. It helps you clean data, explore hypotheses, generate analyses, and produce reproducible artifacts. The target isn't a one-off notebook. It's an analysis that other people can review, trust, and rerun.</p> <h2 id=\"define-your-use-case\">Define your use case</h2> <p>Choose one concrete question you want to answer with your data. The more specific the question, the easier it is to identify the right inputs, checks, and result.</p> <h3 id=\"running-example-property-values-near-the-highway\">Running example: Property values near the highway</h3> <p>As an example, we'll explore the following question:</p> <blockquote> <p>To what extent are houses near the highway lower in property valuation?</p> </blockquote> <p>Suppose one dataset contains property values or sale prices, and another contains location, parcel, or highway-proximity information. The work isn't only to run a model. It's to make the inputs trustworthy, document the joins, pressure-test the result, and end with an artifact that somebody else can use.</p> <p>You can attach CSVs or Excel workbooks, name an approved Google Sheet with <code>@google-drive</code>, or use the desktop app when your data is stored on your computer.</p> <h3 id=\"example-result\">Example result</h3> <p>In a fictional sample, ChatGPT matches 11 property sales to the highway-distance file and flags one sale without a matching distance. Homes within one mile of the highway average <strong>$500,000</strong>, compared with <strong>$600,000</strong> for homes two to five miles away.</p> <p>After excluding the highest-priced distant property, the difference remains <strong>$94,000</strong>. The report and chart explain that the sample is small, the unmatched sale is excluded, and the comparison doesn't establish causation or control for neighborhood, sale timing, traffic, or noise.</p> <h2 id=\"import-the-data\">Import the data</h2> <p>Start by attaching the files and asking ChatGPT to inspect them. This helps answer basic but important questions:</p> <ul> <li>What file formats are here?</li> <li>What does each dataset seem to represent?</li> <li>Which columns might be targets, identifiers, dates, locations, or measures?</li> <li>Where are the clear quality issues?</li> </ul> <p>Don't ask for conclusions yet. Ask for inventory and explanation first.</p> <h2 id=\"tidy-and-merge-the-inputs\">Tidy and merge the inputs</h2> <p>Most real work starts here. You have two or more datasets, the primary key isn't clear, and a naive merge could lose data or create duplicates.</p> <p>Ask ChatGPT to profile the merge before performing it:</p> <ul> <li>Check uniqueness for candidate keys.</li> <li>Measure null rates and formatting differences.</li> <li>Normalize clear formatting issues such as casing, whitespace, or address formatting.</li> <li>Run trial joins and report match rates.</li> <li>Recommend the safest merge strategy before it writes the final merged file.</li> </ul> <p>If you need to derive the best key, such as a normalized address, a parcel identifier built from a few columns, or a location join, ask ChatGPT to explain the tradeoffs and edge cases before you accept the merge.</p> <h2 id=\"explore-with-charts\">Explore with charts</h2> <p>Use charts to understand the data before choosing a model. In the running example, compare homes near the highway with homes farther away, examine outliers, inspect missing-value patterns, and check whether the apparent effect reflects neighborhood composition, home size, or another factor.</p> <p>Keep each chart tied to the original question. Save the useful comparisons so another person can inspect the analysis.</p> <h2 id=\"model-the-question\">Model the question</h2> <p>Not every analysis needs a complex model. Start with an interpretable baseline.</p> <p>For the highway question, a sensible first pass is a regression or other transparent model that estimates the relationship between highway proximity and property value while controlling for relevant factors such as size, age, and location.</p> <p>Ask ChatGPT to be explicit about:</p> <ul> <li>The target variable and feature definitions.</li> <li>Which controls to include and why.</li> <li>Leakage risks and exclusions.</li> <li>How it chose the split, evaluation, or uncertainty estimate.</li> <li>What the result means in plain language.</li> </ul> <p>If the first model is weak, that's still useful. It tells you whether the problem is the model, the features, the join quality, or the question itself.</p> <h2 id=\"communicate-the-result\">Communicate the result</h2> <p>The analysis is only useful when someone else can consume it. Ask ChatGPT to produce the artifact the audience needs:</p> <ul> <li>A Markdown memo for technical collaborators.</li> <li>A spreadsheet or CSV for downstream operations.</li> <li>A formatted document or PDF for decision-makers.</li> <li>A notebook, dashboard, or static report for a reusable analysis.</li> </ul> <p>Ask it to include caveats. If the join quality is imperfect, sampling bias is present, or model assumptions are fragile, the deliverable should say so plainly.</p> <h2 id=\"optional-set-up-a-python-environment\">Optional: set up a Python environment</h2> <p>If the project needs reusable scripts or a notebook, ask ChatGPT to use the existing Python environment or set up a small, reproducible one. Keep source files unchanged and save the analysis, charts, and final report separately. You don't need to set up Python before analyzing attached files in ChatGPT Work.</p> <h2 id=\"suggested-prompts\">Suggested prompts</h2> <p><strong>Load the datasets and explain them</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the data files I've attached and explain what each one contains. Identify likely target columns, dates, parcel or location identifiers, file formats, missing information, and obvious quality issues. Don't draw conclusions yet.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Check the merge before joining</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check how these datasets should be joined. Profile the candidate keys, show duplicate and unmatched records, normalize obvious formatting issues, and explain the safest join. Don't invent missing values or overwrite the source files.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Build an interpretable first model</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Model whether highway proximity is associated with lower property values. Start with an interpretable baseline, account for home size, age, and neighborhood where the data supports it, and explain the effect, uncertainty, and limitations in plain language.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Package the results for stakeholders</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this analysis into a short, stakeholder-ready report. Put the answer first, include the most useful supporting charts, explain the data and join checks, and clearly flag any limitations or uncertainty. Keep the source data unchanged and name the files you create.\n</code></pre>"};
